@NVIDIA/mcore-oncall The design proposal in #2919 checkpoints compute_mappings, but the implementation calls it directly: `h_pre, h_post, h_res = self.compute_mappings(hs_for_mappings)`. Was this intentional due to correctness or performance concerns?

The docstring says its outputs are needed downstream, but couldn't the manager discard them after forward consumption and restore them before backward? Checkpointing could also avoid retaining a full FP32 input copy on paths that upcast the residual stream.

