## Description

At long context the sequence lengths in a decode batch differ widely. The trtllm-gen generation kernel splits each sequence's KV over `smCount / (batch x kvHeads)` CTAs, one CTA per SM. That split assumes equal lengths. A Muse Spark Open attention-DP batch of 6 or more sequences (16 KV heads per rank) therefore gets one CTA per (sequence, KV head). The launch then lasts as long as the one CTA streaming the longest sequence, at about 40 GB/s. At 1M context the full-attention decode FMHA ran at 1.5-2.2 TB/s on GB300 and took 12-27 ms of a 54 ms DEP8 decode

